  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">AUC  Building Capacity for a Results-Oriented Engagement between the AUC and RECs on IDA-Supported Economic Development Areas</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">&quot;Title -Building Capacity of the AUC Chairperson&#x2019;s Office for Stakeholder Outreach in IDA-Supported Economic Development Areas  Development Objective:  Strengthen the capacity of the African Union Commission Chairperson&#x2019;s Office (AUCO) to plan and implement a communication and stakeholder outreach program (e.g. with Regional Economic Communities (RECs)) in order to facilitate the economic development of the Member States (MS). Description of the IDF-financed Components, Activities and Outcomes: &#x2022;	Capacity building for the Chairperson&#x2019;s Office to design and launch a communication and outreach program to mobilize RECs and other stakeholders in supporting the economic development of the member states on IDA priority areas. The component would support the following activities: (a) technical assistance in designing stakeholder surveys and outreach; (b) training on surveys and stakeholder outreach; and (c) technical assistance in implementing stakeholder surveys and outreach programs in priority economic development areas (e.g. regional integration and natural resource management) via consultations, workshops, focus groups and surveys. &#x2022;	Knowledge sharing for senior AUC staff with sister institutions (e.g. OAS, ASEAN, RECs) to compare stakeholder outreach and communication strategies. The component will fund technical exchange visits to coordinate, consult and share knowledge on priority economic development areas.  &#x2022;	Capacity building for dissemination of survey results and IDA priority areas (e.g. via the AUC website). The component would support the following activities: (a) technical assistance in upgrading the AUC website and ICT capability; (b) providing dissemination materials (multi-media and paper-based), survey tools, and equipment and support for translation; and (c) technical assistance for monitoring, evaluation, and dissemination.&quot;</narrative>
  </description>
